<title>JAPAN: Japan industry body sees huge DVD market by 2000.</title>
<headline>Japan industry body sees huge DVD market by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Japanese electronics industry body said on Tuesday it expected the market for next-generation digital video discs (DVDs) in Japan and the United States to total 1.32 trillion yen by 2000.  </p>
<p>The Electronics Industries Association of Japan said it expects the U.S. market to account for 709.1 billion yen, and the Japanese market for the rest by 2000.</p>
<p>The industry body said it made the estimates based on research from Japanese and U.S. content makers.</p>
<p>The group said it expects sales of DVD equipment, including video players, audio players, car audio/video players, game players and ROM and RAM drives, to total 47.1 million units in the two countries by 2000.</p>
</text>
